cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ipldt or ORMIR-BQRL, please cite the paper below and this software."
title: "ipldt 1.0.0 and ORMIR-BQRL 0.1.0: an open-source reimplementation of the Scanco IPL bone morphometry evaluation for XtremeCT II"
abstract: "ipldt 1.0.0 is an open-source Python reimplementation of the bone morphometry evaluation that Scanco's Image Processing Language (IPL V5.42) runs on XtremeCT II HR-pQCT scans; ORMIR-BQRL 0.1.0 is the workflow built on it (one command from a Scanco AIM to masks, segmentation, cortical pore map, distance-transform maps and a report, with manual correction in 3D Slicer and re-entry). Both are released together in this repository."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-25
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zhuyihua1234/ipldt"
keywords:
  - HR-pQCT
  - XtremeCT II
  - bone microarchitecture
  - Image Processing Language
  - Laplace-Hamming
  - distance transform
  - trabecular thickness
  - ORMIR
authors:
